(global_label "NMEA_SHIELD" (shape passive) (at 320.04 143.51 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "28518c1e-5a43-4337-b70b-ee67633ec96d"))
(wire (pts (xy 320.04 153.67) (xy 320.04 156.21)) (stroke (width 0) (type default)) (uuid "74d4bf82-b57d-46e5-a26e-d3228753eb25"))
(global_label "GND_CAN" (shape passive) (at 320.04 156.21 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "9468f084-f71d-471d-a002-0d73f7b074ff"))
(text "ISO1042 primary is 3.3 V. VCC2 must be 4.5 V to 5.5 V, so U9 is a Murata MEJ2S0305SC, 3.3 V to 5 V, 400 mA rating.\\nR94 is 120 ohm, about 42 mA, just over 10 percent of that rating. Measure ISO_5V at that preload. It has to sit inside 4.5 V to 5.5 V. Do not treat a 9 percent envelope or 5.45 V as a shown Murata number.\\nHipot 5.2 kVDC for 1 s. Continuous functional barrier 2.4 kVDC. Not a safety barrier.\\nJP1 open: R90 holds CAN_VIN low, the module is off, and R91 lets GPIO18 read low. JP1 fitted: the module runs and GPIO18 reads high.\\nR91 limits a mistaken GPIO drive to about 0.3 mA. There is no 120 ohm between CAN_H and CAN_L. R94 is a preload, not a terminator.\\nC92 joins the shield to GND_CAN only. Do not land the NMEA NET-S wire." (at 20 70 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27))) (uuid "f4bfaadf-490e-4c2b-b415-9f4f69c917b7"))
  (embedded_fonts no)
)
